<title>LATVIA: CENTRAL BANK GOLD AND FOREIGN RESERVES UP IN JULY.</title>
<headline>CENTRAL BANK GOLD AND FOREIGN RESERVES UP IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's central bank said on Tuesday that its gold and foreign reserves rose in July by 15 million lats to 546.19 million lats.</p>
<p>The bank added in a statement that the amount of lats in circulation rose by 1.2 percent to 313.825 million lats.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
